    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0444" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to The British Secretary of State for
                        Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eden</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d218-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-28">December 28, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6080. Your telegram Taut 185.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d218-f2"/> My immediately
                    following telegram gives text of declaration which President has re-drafted, and
                    which Prime Minister has approved. He realises that the order of mention of
                    Governments is not as we should have it, but President pressed this
                    arrangement.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>State Department are giving it to foreign representatives concerned to
                        secure approval from their Governments.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I am doing the same on Prime Minister’s instructions to Dominion
                        representatives, including Mr. Langstone for New Zealand.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>I am awaiting telegram in reply to my telephone message to Bridges about
                        India. Prime Minister and President both anxious to include India,
                        especially in view of war developments.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
